From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pblsketch <239486537+pblsketch@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 25/30] fix(layout): 글 있는 문단을 끝내는 문단 기준 위아래 표 뒤 첫 줄을 표 아래끝에 둔다

What Hangul does: when a paragraph-relative topAndBottom table ends the flow
of a paragraph that has text, Hangul 2024 starts the next paragraph's first
line exactly at the table's bottom (outer bottom margin included). It adds
neither the host's space after nor the next paragraph's space before. Its own
saved line ladder says the same: the next paragraph's stored vpos equals the
table frame bottom (fixture para-float-tail-table: 15577 = 5220 + 1100 + 9257;
27469 child-allowance pi=24: 51781; 20260909-para-table pi=2: 55291). Only
documents saved for MS Word compatibility (HWP compatible-document target 2,
HWPX applyPrevspacingBeneathObject) are laid out differently.

What devel did: 0028 kept only half of this (no host space after). The next
paragraph still took its own space before, 4px on the app fixture. The other
half, pinning `stored_successor_line_origin` to the table bottom, had been
dropped because it broke issue_6718 page 4 (102px past the body) and
issue_6950. The cause was not the pin or the ladder binding: in both
documents the stored ladder agrees with the pin. Typeset emits a text-tail
table before its own host lines (#6950 paint order), and paint consumed the
successor origin right after the table item (`layout_table_item`), so the
host's own lines restarted below the table.

What changes:
- typeset/table/block/entry.rs: a NextLine placement of a paragraph with
  text gets `stored_successor_line_origin = occupied_bottom`, unless the
  document applies the previous spacing beneath objects (MS Word target).
- layout.rs: the table item consumes the successor origin only when no
  later item of the same paragraph follows in its column. Otherwise the
  paragraph's completion consumes it (`paragraph_end` already does).
- model: bring back `applies_prev_spacing_beneath_object` and the profile
  flag `prev_spacing_beneath_object` from the old 0028.

Evidence (Hangul 2024 13.0.0.711 print through the official automation):
- para-float-tail-table.hwpx page 2: next line top - table bottom
  Hangul 0 (ink 333.5 vs table bottom 332.4), devel 8.0, before this 4.0,
  now 0.0. The line after it: Hangul ~355.2, now 355.6. The table stays
  1100HU (14.7px) below the host's second line.
- 27469-child-allowance-retroactive-support.hwp page 4: the first line of
  the paragraph after the empty one sits 54.6px under the table in Hangul,
  68.2px before this, 54.9px now. Page count stays 12.
- 20260909-para-table.hwpx: no change (next paragraph has no space before).
- Over samples/ (1423 documents), the pin fires on 20 tables; it moves
  lines only where the next paragraph has space before (the two above).
- The 50 documents of the private overlap set render identically.
- An MS Word target variant of the fixture: Hangul lays the whole paragraph
  out differently (the host's second line goes below the table), so it is
  not pinned here.
